# Cursor Rules

## Main Purpose

- **Primary Goal**: This website (video2gifapp.com) is a landing page and how-to guide site for the iOS app Make Video to GIF, a video to GIF converter for iPhone with trim, crop, frames per second, loop count and encoder controls and on-device export (https://apps.apple.com/app/id6762465120). Facts about the app live in `app.md`. All content, design, and functionality should be optimized to promote and drive downloads of the iOS app. There is deliberately no online converter on the site: the site answers iPhone-specific questions and sends readers to the app.

## File Modification Rules

- **DO NOT** modify `index.html` - it is a generated file. All HTML changes should be made in `build/template.html` instead.
- When making changes to the template, update `build/template.html` and regenerate the HTML files using the build script.

## Project Structure

- `build/template.html` - Main template file for generating HTML
- `build/build.js` - Build script that generates HTML from template
- `build/*.json` - Page copy per language (`en.json` is the source; add a locale by creating `build/<code>.json` and listing it in `LANGUAGES` in `build/constants.js`)
- `build/constants.js` - Site URL, App Store id, languages, guide config, IndexNow key
- `build/partials/*.html` - Shared head, header, footer, App Store button, analytics
- `build/guides/*.json` - Optional SEO guide pages (one JSON per keyword) rendered with `build/guide-template.html`
- `index.html` - Generated file for English (do not edit directly)
- `*/index.html` - Generated files for language-specific pages - do not edit directly
- `llms.txt`, `urls.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt` - Generated by `npm run build` / `npm run sitemap`
- `img/` - App icon, favicons, QR code and App Store screenshots (downloaded from the App Store listing; replace the files by hand when the listing changes)
- `style.css` - Main stylesheet
- `privacy.html` - Privacy policy page
- `terms.html` - Terms of service page
- `package.json` - Node.js dependencies and scripts
- `fonts/` - Self-hosted Pixelify Sans (display) and Onest (text) woff2 subsets; `@font-face` rules live at the top of `style.css`. No Google Fonts requests.
- `img/gif-demo-sprite.png` - 8-frame 64×48 pixel-art sprite for the hero GIF player and timeline (stepped by `site.js` at the chosen FPS, scaled with `image-rendering: pixelated`)

## Design rules

- Palette (indexed, six colors): plum #2a1b47, pink #f0186f, teal #3fd0c4, green #2fb344, sun #ffc83d, checker #efebf5 on white.
- Pixelify Sans only for h1/h2 and short display labels; numbers and body text in Onest (Pixelify's 8, B and G are too easy to confuse).
- Stepped "pixel" corners (`--notch`, `--notch-2`) instead of border-radius; no drop shadows.
- The hero GIF player is the one loud element; keep other sections quiet.
